//RS 
//RS /// D-JPK-DISPATCH1=B (A1, card c9jetpackgates): `jet` execs the engine
//RS /// binary (`jetpack`, later `jetos`) for every engine verb instead of linking
//RS /// it in-process — git/kubectl-style dispatch by executable name. Before
//RS /// exec-ing the real command, `jet` runs `<engine> --engine-protocol`, a
//RS /// hidden handshake flag every engine binary answers with its own
//RS /// `CARGO_PKG_VERSION` on stdout; a mismatch against `jet`'s own version is
//RS /// E1227 (`engine-version-skew`). This is process-dispatch plumbing between
//RS /// two binaries jet ships together, never a token a user writes in a `.jet`
//RS /// file, so I7 (every user-typeable keyword lives here with a decision ID)
//RS /// does not require it to gate a Tower ballot of its own — it is this
//RS /// gate's own implementation surface.
//RS pub const ENGINE_PROTOCOL_FLAG: &str = "--engine-protocol";
//RS 
