//RS 
//RS /// D-JPK-SERVICE1 (supervised-services slice, card c9jetpackgates):
//RS /// the recognized fields of a **dev-supervised** `Service` (an entry under an
//RS /// `env.<name>` role-module's `services:` map). `Service` stays the one
//RS /// ratified open record either way (same grammar as `system.*.services`,
//RS /// `SYSTEM_FIELD_SERVICES`/`SERVICE_FIELD_ENABLE` reused verbatim) — only the
//RS /// dev-runtime tier (`Jetpack::Services`) interprets these particular keys,
//RS /// to start/probe/stop the supervised process: `ports` (the `[Int]` TCP ports
//RS /// it listens on), `run` (the executable plus argv that starts it), `shutdown`
//RS /// (the typed stop policy, else a bounded signal sequence), `data_dir` (its
//RS /// persisted-state directory, else `.jet/services/<name>/data`), and `ready`
//RS /// (a shell command polled until it exits 0 — the readiness contract, else a
//RS /// TCP probe on `ports[0]`, else a bare process-alive check). Dependencies use
//RS /// `after` only; retired `depends_on` declarations are rejected by the dev
//RS /// supervisor as E1262.
//RS pub const DEV_SERVICE_FIELD_PORTS: &str = "ports";
